WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.302 --> 00:00:06.308
On Wednesday I returned to Miss Havisham's. I rang the bell at the gate, and Estella

2
00:00:06.309 --> 00:00:11.108
came across the courtyard. After letting me in, she locked the gate and led me into the

3
00:00:11.109 --> 00:00:14.774
dark passage where I had been before. As we walked along the passage, she suddenly stopped

4
00:00:14.775 --> 00:00:18.213
and turned to me. "Well?" she said with her face quite close to mine. "Well, miss,"

5
00:00:18.214 --> 00:00:21.515
I replied, almost falling over her. "Am I pretty?" "Yes, I think you're very pretty." "Am

6
00:00:21.516 --> 00:00:26.452
I insulting?" "Not so much as you were last time," I said. "No?" She raised her hand

7
00:00:26.453 --> 00:00:29.618
and slapped my face. "Now, you coarse, little monster, what do you think of me?" "I

8
00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:36.436
won't tell you." "Because you're going to tell Miss Havisham?" "No, that's not it." "Why don't

9
00:00:36.437 --> 00:00:38.086
you cry again, you little wretch?" "I'll never cry for you again." But I knew this was

10
00:00:38.087 --> 00:00:40.690
false because I was already holding back my tears. We went on our way after that,

11
00:00:40.691 --> 00:00:42.515
and on the stairs we met a gentleman coming down. "Who do we have here?" asked

12
00:00:42.516 --> 00:00:45.078
the gentleman, looking at me. "A boy," said Estella. He was a burly man with a dark

13
00:00:45.079 --> 00:00:51.015
complexion. He took my chin in his hand and turned my face to have a look

14
00:00:51.016 --> 00:00:55.263
at me by the light of Estella's candle. "A boy from the neighborhood, eh?" he said.

15
00:00:55.264 --> 00:00:58.842
"How do you come to be here?" "Miss Havisham sent for me, sir." "Well, behave yourself!

16
00:00:58.843 --> 00:01:01.009
I have a good deal of experience with boys, and they're all bad." With these words, he

17
00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:08.651
released me—which I was glad of because his hand smelled of scented soap—and went downstairs. There

18
00:01:08.652 --> 00:01:13.405
was no time to wonder who he was because Estella soon left me at the door

19
00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.580
to Miss Havisham's room. I went in and Miss Havisham asked if I was ready to play.

20
00:01:15.581 --> 00:01:21.151
"I don't think I am, ma'am." "Then you are willing to work?" I nodded and she

21
00:01:21.152 --> 00:01:27.476
directed me to wait for her in the room across the passage. I entered the room

22
00:01:27.477 --> 00:01:32.373
and found that it had also been sealed against the daylight. It was a spacious room,

23
00:01:32.374 --> 00:01:35.722
which had probably been handsome once. But everything in it was now covered with dust and mold

24
00:01:35.723 --> 00:01:39.722
and was falling to pieces. The most prominent object was a long table with a tablecloth

25
00:01:39.723 --> 00:01:43.786
spread over it as if a feast were being prepared when the house and the clocks

26
00:01:43.787 --> 00:01:47.794
all stopped together. There was a centerpiece of some kind in the middle of the table. It

27
00:01:47.795 --> 00:01:51.294
was so heavily overhung with cobwebs that I could not tell exactly what it was. Spiders

28
00:01:51.295 --> 00:01:56.183
were running in and out of it as if something of great importance had just happened

29
00:01:56.184 --> 00:02:04.858
in the spider world. Miss Havisham entered the room and pointed to this strange object with

30
00:02:04.859 --> 00:02:08.358
her walking stick. "What do you think that is?" "I can't guess, ma'am." "It is a great

31
00:02:08.359 --> 00:02:13.025
cake. A wedding cake. Mine!" Before I could react, she said, "Come. Walk me!" She laid

32
00:02:13.026 --> 00:02:18.842
her hand on my shoulder, and I slowly walked her around the room. "Today is my

33
00:02:18.843 --> 00:02:25.509
birthday, Pip." I was going to wish her happiness, but she said, "I don't let anyone mention

34
00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:27.255
it. On this day, long before you were born, this heap of decay was brought here."

35
00:02:27.256 --> 00:02:31.675
She stabbed at the pile of cobwebs on the table with her stick, but didn't touch

36
00:02:31.676 --> 00:02:39.494
it. "When the ruin is complete and they lay me dead in my wedding dress on this

37
00:02:39.495 --> 00:02:41.556
table, that will be the final curse on him. Call Estella!" I didn't dare to ask

38
00:02:41.557 --> 00:02:50.580
who he was. Estella appeared and Miss Havisham said she wanted to see us play cards

39
00:02:50.581 --> 00:02:55.413
again. So we returned to her room and sat down. Again Miss Havisham watched us the

40
00:02:55.414 --> 00:03:03.389
whole time, directing my attention to Estella's beauty and the loveliness of her jewels against Estella's hair.

41
00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:12.881
Estella did not bother to speak. After we played six games, a day was selected for

42
00:03:12.882 --> 00:03:20.215
my return. Estella again took me down into the courtyard to be fed like a dog.

43
00:03:20.216 --> 00:03:26.119
Then I was left to wander about as I liked. I strolled through a miserable, neglected garden

44
00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:32.635
and a greenhouse with nothing in it but a fallen-down grapevine and some bottles. I came

45
00:03:32.636 --> 00:03:39.627
upon a small, detached house that might have belonged to the brewery manager. I peered in

46
00:03:39.628 --> 00:03:44.611
a window, and to my great surprise, a pale young gentleman looked up from his studying

47
00:03:44.612 --> 00:03:53.024
and stared at me. He quickly came outside. "Hello," he said. "Who let you in?" "Miss Estella."

48
00:03:53.025 --> 00:03:56.428
"And who gave you permission to prowl about?" "Miss Estella." "Come and fight." His manner was

49
00:03:56.429 --> 00:03:57.936
so final—and I was so astonished—that I followed him as if I were under a spell.

50
00:03:57.937 --> 00:04:00.333
"Wait a minute," he said, turning around before we had gone too many paces. "I should give

51
00:04:00.334 --> 00:04:01.762
you a reason for fighting." Before I could respond, he butted his head into my stomach!

52
00:04:01.763 --> 00:04:03.270
I swung my fist at him and missed. He dodged backward and forward and did all

53
00:04:03.271 --> 00:04:08.762
sorts of things while I looked helplessly at him. "Hold on!" He left for a moment

54
00:04:08.763 --> 00:04:15.587
and quickly returned with a bottle of water and a sponge. "For both of us," he said,

55
00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:21.492
placing these items on the ground. And then he pulled off not only his jacket and

56
00:04:21.493 --> 00:04:26.579
waistcoat but also his shirt. I removed my shirt too. My heart failed me when I

57
00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:31.572
saw him raise his fists and look me over as if he were choosing which bone to

58
00:04:31.573 --> 00:04:35.651
break. So I was very surprised when I struck the first blow and he ended up

59
00:04:35.652 --> 00:04:41.397
on the ground with a bloody nose. But he got back on his feet, and after

60
00:04:41.398 --> 00:04:47.048
sponging himself off, was ready to fight again. Imagine my surprise when he landed on his back

61
00:04:47.049 --> 00:04:52.310
again, this time with a black eye. His spirit made me feel great respect for him.

62
00:04:52.311 --> 00:04:56.953
He never once hit me hard, and he was always knocked down, but he would be

63
00:04:56.954 --> 00:05:04.969
up again in an instant, sponging himself or drinking from the water bottle. He got heavily

64
00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:12.866
bruised, for I am sorry to say that I hit him hard. At last he gave up

65
00:05:12.867 --> 00:05:17.048
and admitted that I had won. As I got dressed, I felt only a gloomy satisfaction

66
00:05:17.049 --> 00:05:26.111
in my victory. "Can I help you?" I asked him. "No, thank you. Good afternoon." And

67
00:05:26.112 --> 00:05:30.286
he went back inside. When I returned to the courtyard, I found Estella waiting for me, looking

68
00:05:30.287 --> 00:05:34.938
strangely happy. But instead of going straight to the gate, she stepped back into the house

69
00:05:34.939 --> 00:05:39.508
and beckoned me. "Come here. You may kiss me if you like." I kissed her cheek

70
00:05:39.509 --> 00:05:42.274
as she turned it to me. I think I would have gone through a great deal

71
00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:47.589
to kiss that cheek. But I felt she gave that kiss to a coarse, common boy in

72
00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:55.255
the same way that she might have given him money. As if it were worth nothing.

